🔁 7. What Happens When You Delete?
If you delete a record:

Oracle removes that key from the leaf.

If leaf becomes too empty, Oracle merges it with its neighbor (called coalesce).

It may also remove or update branch keys.

Tree always stays balanced — that’s the “B” in B-tree.

